{"name":"Armagnac","hex":"#ad916c","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Armagnac","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A region and former county of the duchy of Gascony in modern-day France.","A party prominent in French politics and warfare during the Hundred Years' War."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A brandy made in the region of Armagnac."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Armagnac"}],"entries":[{"title":"Armagnac","blocks":[{"text":"Armagnac is a brandy produced in the Armagnac region in Gascony, southwest France. It is distilled from wine usually made from a blend of grapes including Baco 22A, Colombard, Folle blanche and Ugni blanc, traditionally using column stills. This is in contrast to the pot stills used in the production of Cognac, which is made predominantly from Ugni blanc grapes. The resulting spirit is aged in oak barrels before release. Production is overseen by the Institut national de l'origine et de la qualité (INAO) and the Bureau National Interprofessionel de l'Armagnac (BNIA)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Armagnac-img_0465.jpg/330px-Armagnac-img_0465.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Armagnac","wikidata":"Q503252"},{"title":"Armagnac (party)","blocks":[{"text":"The Armagnac faction was prominent in French politics and warfare during the Hundred Years' War. It was allied with the supporters of Charles I, Duke of Orléans against John the Fearless after Charles' father Louis of Orléans was killed on a Paris street on the orders of the Duke of Burgundy on 23 November 1407."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Les_Tr%C3%A8s_Riches_Heures_du_duc_de_Berry_avril.jpg/330px-Les_Tr%C3%A8s_Riches_Heures_du_duc_de_Berry_avril.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Armagnac_(party)","wikidata":"Q301905"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Vignoble_d%27Armagnac.JPG/500px-Vignoble_d%27Armagnac.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Vignoble_d%27Armagnac.JPG/1280px-Vignoble_d%27Armagnac.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Vignoble_d%27Armagnac.JPG/500px-Vignoble_d%27Armagnac.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Vineyards in the Armagnac region near Landes and Gers","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVignoble_d'Armagnac.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/The_Armagnac_Region%2C_France.jpg/500px-The_Armagnac_Region%2C_France.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/The_Armagnac_Region%2C_France.jpg/1280px-The_Armagnac_Region%2C_France.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/The_Armagnac_Region%2C_France.jpg/500px-The_Armagnac_Region%2C_France.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Map of the Armagnac region.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Armagnac_Region%2C_France.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Arthez_alambic_Ognoas_1936.jpg/500px-Arthez_alambic_Ognoas_1936.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Arthez_alambic_Ognoas_1936.jpg/1280px-Arthez_alambic_Ognoas_1936.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Arthez_alambic_Ognoas_1936.jpg/50